<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Portable SmartHub bridge + discovery core for the OpenBurnBar Windows port
    (Phase 4 · integrations lane). This is the DEPENDENCY-FREE half of the
    SmartHub Nest-Hub bridge and LAN discovery:

      * Bridge/ — the on-device dashboard bridge's REQUEST->RESPONSE core:
        the HTTP/1.1 request parser, the constant-time bridge-token access
        control (query token OR bearer header), the /state.json contract
        renderer (byte-for-byte with the Swift emitter), the snapshot +
        per-display config models, and the pure route dispatcher. The LIVE
        socket listener is the only thing that lives in the Net adapter.
      * Discovery/ — DNS-SD / mDNS record build + parse (RFC 1035 / 2782 / 6763):
        name encode/decode with compression, PTR/SRV/TXT/A rdata, full message
        assemble/parse, the OpenBurnBar hub advertisement + browse-and-resolve
        helpers, and the IPv4 subnet-candidate + LAN-usability math. The live
        UDP multicast socket lives in the Net adapter; NetService/Bonjour on
        macOS hides these bytes, so the wire format is authored + proven here.

    It has NO WinUI / Windows / socket dependency on purpose — the SAME managed
    assembly is referenced by the Net adapter (HttpListener + UdpClient) AND
    unit-tested on the macOS authoring host today via `dotnet test`
    (windows/tests/integrations), mirroring the OpenBurnBar.Pal.Ipc portable-core
    pattern (VAL-P0-CONPTY-018).

    Parity sources (macOS):
      * AgentLens/Services/SmartHub/SmartHubBridgeServer.swift
          -> Bridge/BridgeHttpParser.cs + BridgeAccessControl.cs + BridgeRouter.cs
             + BridgeStateJson.cs + BridgeWireFormat.cs + SmartHubBridgeSnapshot.cs
      * OpenBurnBarCore/.../SharedModels/SmartHubDisplayConfig.swift
          -> Bridge/SmartHubDisplayConfig.cs
      * OpenBurnBarCore/.../SharedModels/SmartHubConfig.swift (SmartHubTimePeriod)
          -> Bridge/SmartHubTimePeriod.cs
      * AgentLens/Services/SmartHub/LocalNetworkDiscovery.swift
          -> Discovery/Ipv4Subnet.cs (portable IPv4/subnet math)
      * NetService/Bonjour advertise+browse (opaque on macOS)
          -> Discovery/DnsName.cs + DnsRecords.cs + DnsMessage.cs + MdnsAdvertisement.cs

    Targets net8.0 so a net8.0-windows WinUI app can reference it; net10.0 adapter
    + tests reference it too. Zero external package references.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.Integrations.SmartHub</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.Integrations.SmartHub</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
